        "title": "fix(twitch): time out Helix user resolution lookups",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users resolving Twitch targets could wait indefinitely when Helix user lookup requests stalled.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Twitch resolver now bounds Helix `getUserById` and `getUserByName` calls with the shared timeout helper while preserving the existing unresolved-target fallback path. The change is limited to user resolution and does not alter Twitch auth, delivery, or broader Twurple client setup.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted contribution prepared for Alix-007.\n\n## User Impact\n\nA stalled Twitch lookup now fails quickly enough for the resolver to return the existing not-resolved result instead of leaving setup or target resolution hanging.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/twitch/src/resolver.test.ts`\n- Result: 1 test file passed, 2 tests passed.\n- `git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD --`\n- Result: passed.\n",
